      "ordering_key": 2,
      "per_curiam": false,
      "sha1": "",
      "snippet": "\nUtter, C.J.\n(concurring and dissenting) \u2014 As the majority explains, difficult line-drawing and careful adjustment of burdens of proof are necessary in order to resolve the inherent conflict between the public's constitutionally protected interest in open pretrial proceedings and the criminal defendant's constitutional right to a fair trial. Although agreeing with the majority's statement of ",
