      "snippet": "\nLau, J.\n\u00b61 We are asked to determine the correct legal standard to apply when ruling on a motion to seal court records for a vacated criminal conviction under the current version of General Rule (GR) 15. Karen Waldon sought to have her 1985 theft conviction vacated and the court record sealed to assist her in finding new employment. Opposing Waldon\u2019s motion to seal, the State argued that trial courts are constitutionally required",
      "type": "lead-opinion"
    }
